<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04PH">Exercise <span data-tag="04PH">9.6.0.5</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{Set}$ denote the category of sets, let $\mathrm{Surj}$ be the collection of surjective functions, and let $\mathrm{Inj}$ be the collection of injective functions. Show that: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The pair $(\mathrm{Surj}, \mathrm{Inj} )$ is a factorization system on $\operatorname{Set}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The pair $( \mathrm{Inj}, \mathrm{Surj})$ is a weak factorization system on $\operatorname{Set}$ which is not a factorization system. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> See Exercise <a data-tag="04NS" href="/tag/04NS">9.6.6.22</a>. </p>
